s a bounded below complex of injectives.\nNote that <MATH_0003> is K-injective\n(Derived Categories, Lemma\n<REF_0001>).\nHence the construction in Section <REF_0002>\nshows that\n<MATH_0004> is \nrepresented by the complex <MATH_0005> with terms\n<MATH_0006>\n(equality because there are only finitely many nonzero terms).\nNote that <MATH_0007> is the total complex associated to\nthe double complex with terms\n<MATH_0008>\nand similarly for <MATH_0009>.\nThe natural map <MATH_0010>\ncomes from a map of double complexes.\nThus to show this map is a quasi-isomorphism, we may use the spectral\nsequence of a double complex\n(Homology, Lemma <REF_0003>)\n<MATH_0011>\nconverging to <MATH_0012> and similarly for\n<MATH_0013>. To finish the proof of the lemma it\nsuffices to show that <MATH_0014>\ninduces an isomorphism\n<MATH_0015>\non cohomology sheaves whenever <MATH_0016> is a direct summand of a\nfinite free <MATH_0017>-module. Since this is clear when <MATH_0018>\nis finite free the result follows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b4717756778c7bfbd384a13f1d11ac9b7787258aa66f7eea38380553fe7b04c", "unit_id": "tag:08JI:proof"}
